== a_histogram_without_a_variable
error[Z0406]: `histogram` needs `var`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | d.histogram()
  |   ^^^^^^^^^ `var` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.histogram(var, bins: Int | sturges | scott | fd = fd, binwidth: Float, start: Float, scale: count | density | fraction | percent = count, by: Var | Vars)`

== a_histogram_of_text
error[Z0401]: `histogram` counts the rows in bins along `x`, but the `x` axis of this plot holds the categories of `name`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | d.histogram(name)
  |   ^^^^^^^^^ needs numbers along `x`
  |
  = help: `points` and `lines` are placed on an axis of categories; `histogram` needs a number along `x`

== a_histogram_of_a_variable_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `scores` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | d.histogram(scores)
  |             ^^^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: did you mean `score`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"score"`

== a_histogram_with_no_bin
error[Z0401]: `bins:` of `histogram` is how many bins there are, 1 or more, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:26
  |
3 | d.histogram(score, bins: 0)
  |                          ^ not a number of bins
  |
  = help: write a whole number, as in `bins: 30`, or a rule that gives one from the values: `sturges`, `scott` or `fd`

== a_histogram_with_a_rule_that_is_none
error[Z0402]: `knuth` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:26
  |
3 | d.histogram(score, bins: knuth)
  |                          ^^^^^ expected one of sturges, scott, fd, or an Int

== a_histogram_in_panels_by_a_variable_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `site` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:24
  |
3 | d.histogram(score, by: site)
  |                        ^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: the variables of `d` are: score, arm, name, read, day

== a_histogram_with_a_colour
error[Z0404]: `histogram` has no argument called `color`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:20
  |
3 | d.histogram(score, color: arm)
  |                    ^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `data.histogram(var, bins: Int | sturges | scott | fd = fd, binwidth: Float, start: Float, scale: count | density | fraction | percent = count, by: Var | Vars)`

== a_density_of_dates
error[Z0401]: `density` estimates a density along `x`, but the `x` axis of this plot holds the dates of `day`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | d.density(day)
  |   ^^^^^^^ needs numbers along `x`
  |
  = help: `points`, `lines` and `step` are placed on a scale of dates; `density` needs a number along `x`, and may have dates along the other axis

== a_density_with_a_bandwidth_of_nothing
error[Z0401]: `bandwidth:` of `density` is the standard deviation of the kernel in the units of `x`, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:29
  |
3 | d.density(score, bandwidth: 0)
  |                             ^ not above 0
  |
  = help: leave `bandwidth:` out for Silverman's rule of thumb; `adjust: 2` makes the estimate smoother and `adjust: 0.5` rougher

== a_density_coloured_by_a_number
error[Z0401]: `density` draws each line in one colour, so `color` must show categories, but `score` is an Int without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | d.density(score, color: score)
  |   ^^^^^^^ a colour for each row, not for each line
  |
  = help: colour the lines by a variable of categories, as in `density(color: union)`, or set one colour for this layer, as in `density(color: "black")`

== a_boxplot_of_text
error[Z0401]: `boxplot` draws a box over the values of `y`, but the `y` axis of this plot holds the categories of `name`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:3
  |
3 | d.boxplot(name)
  |   ^^^^^^^ needs numbers along `y`
  |
  = help: `points` and `lines` are placed on an axis of categories; `boxplot` needs a number along `y`

